From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Artem Butusov <art.sormy@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 22 Nov 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [GStreamer] A hole-punch quirk hands video frames to the
 embedder

The GPU of a Mali-450 class board cannot draw a 4K, or even a full screen
1080p, video frame within a 60 Hz frame, while its display controller
scales one on a plane for free. With WEBKIT_GST_HOLE_PUNCH_QUIRK=tvbian
the page draws a hole where the video is, and the tvbvideoplanesink
element hands the decoded frames, the hole's rectangle and the page they
belong to to the embedder, which shows them under the page.

A media player learns the identifier of its page, the one
webkit_web_view_get_page_id() returns, to tell the embedder's views apart.

The page's buffer keeps its alpha channel, so the video shows through the
hole.

